<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Vulnerability research, bug bounty writeups, and notes from a pentester building toward OSCP."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-07-25')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Brayden Arnold, a penetration tester working toward OSCP and building a career in
		offensive security. This site is where I write up vulnerability research: coordinated
		disclosures against open source projects, bug bounty findings once they're safe to publish,
		and notes from CTFs and certification study along the way.
	</p>

	<p>
		Everything here is published after a fix ships and the vendor has confirmed it's safe to talk
		about. If you're a maintainer and something here needs a correction, reach out and I'll fix
		it.
	</p>

	<p>
		Find me on <a href="https://github.com/builtbybrayden" target="_blank">GitHub</a> or
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brayden-arnold-5387b3199/" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>
